# Python Environment

When running Python scripts, tests, or tools in this project, **always use the project's virtualenv** (`.venv`).

## Correct usage

Prefer **Make targets** (they use venv + PYTHONPATH):

```bash
make test          # all tests
make test-unit     # unit only
make run           # bot one-shot
make dashboard     # Streamlit
make init-db       # init DB
```

Or explicitly:

```bash
# Run a script (PYTHONPATH so root modules import)
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python scripts/run_cashstra.py

# Run pytest
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -v

# Run a one-off command
PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -c "from src.cashstra.data.storage import init_db; init_db()"
```

## Alternative: activate first

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
python scripts/run_cashstra.py
```

## Do not

- Run `python` or `python3` directly unless the venv is already activated
- Use system Python for project scripts or tests
